# IMP Command Usage :-

1) terraform state list
    : list all resources currently tracked within the Terraform state file.

2) terraform state show [resource_name]
    : It give detail information about your "Single resource"

3) terraform state mv [resource_name].[terraform_identifier_Old_Name]  [resource_name].[New_Name]
    : The terraform state mv command is primarily used for refactoring Terraform configurations 
        without causing disruption to the existing infrastructure. 

4) terraform state pull
    : It show detailed information of "All resources"

5) terraform state rm [resource_name]
    : removes a resource from Terraform's state file 
        without destroying the actual, corresponding real-world infrastructure object.
      The object continues to exist, but Terraform will no longer manage it.
        (This means that if you delete a resource, terraform cannot manage the object created by it.)
      [ex- after this command, the terraform destroy command will not run]
